@lang pt
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cp-dominio`
IMPORT `cp-pena`

-- Código Penal, Título XI, Capítulos II-B, III e IV (arts. 337-E a 359-H):
-- what the group g6b's modules share. No article is encoded here; each noun and
-- helper below is used by more than one of g6b's modules.
--
--   * the attempt, read from cp-dominio's `Execução do crime`: the two facts
--     art. 14, II reads beside an offence's own elements (the execution began;
--     something outside the agent's will stopped it), so every offence that
--     admits an attempt carries them the same way.
--   * `Processo ou procedimento`: the proceedings arts. 339, 342, 343, 344 and
--     347 name, each with its own list. The members are fine-grained so that
--     each article's list can be written as the article writes it; the three
--     helpers below say which members are "processo judicial", "processo
--     civil" and "processo administrativo". One member says there was no proceeding at all.
--   * `Pessoa que funciona no processo`: the persons arts. 342, 343 and 357
--     list, and two members no list names (a party; anyone else).
--
-- Insignificância: STJ Súmula 599 holds it inapplicable to crimes against the
-- public administration (sweep entry M-sweep-c-15, fork F-sweep-c-10, which
-- g6a creates for the whole Título XI). The Súmula's two carve-outs (arts. 334
-- and 334-A) are outside this group's range, so none of g6b's offences takes
-- the judge's finding of insignificance as an input.
--
-- Art. 327, § 2º ("A pena será aumentada da terça parte quando os autores dos
-- crimes previstos neste Capítulo ...") reaches the crimes of Capítulo I only:
-- "neste Capítulo" is the chapter it sits in. No g6b offence carries it (fork
-- F-g6b-01).

§ `Título XI — Dos crimes contra a administração pública (Capítulos II-B, III e IV): o comum do grupo`

§§ `A execução do crime (art. 14, II)`

-- The facts an attempt is read from. `execução iniciada` is TRUE for a
-- consummated crime too; it is the offence's own elements that say whether it
-- was consummated. The record is cp-dominio.l4's `Execução do crime`
-- (integration, 2026-09-30).

-- "Art. 14 - Diz-se o crime: ... II - tentado, quando, iniciada a execução,
-- não se consuma por circunstâncias alheias à vontade do agente."
@ref CP art. 14, II
GIVEN e IS AN `Execução do crime`
      `os elementos do tipo reunidos` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the crime was attempted, on the facts of its execution
`tentativa pelos fatos da execução (art. 14, II)` e `os elementos do tipo reunidos` MEANS
    `crime tentado (art. 14, II)` (e's `execução iniciada`) `os elementos do tipo reunidos` (e's `consumação impedida por circunstâncias alheias à vontade do agente`)

§§ `Processos e procedimentos`

-- The proceedings the chapter names. Art. 339 names six by name; art. 342
-- says "processo judicial, ou administrativo, inquérito policial, ou ... juízo
-- arbitral"; art. 344 "processo judicial, policial ou administrativo, ou ...
-- juízo arbitral"; art. 347 "processo civil ou administrativo" and "processo
-- penal"; arts. 342, § 1º and 343, parágrafo único "processo penal, ou ...
-- processo civil em que for parte entidade da administração pública". A
-- proceeding is recorded as the one member that describes it, and a case with
-- no proceeding at all as `nenhum processo ou procedimento`, which no article's
-- list names. (Art. 347's record says the same with NOTHING, since its
-- "processo penal, ainda que não iniciado" needs no pending proceeding.)
DECLARE `Processo ou procedimento` IS ONE OF
    `inquérito policial`
    @nlg:en a police inquiry
    `procedimento investigatório criminal`
    @nlg:en a criminal investigation procedure (conducted by the public prosecution)
    `processo judicial penal`
    @nlg:en a criminal judicial proceeding
    `ação de improbidade administrativa`
    @nlg:en an action for administrative impropriety
    `outro processo judicial não penal`
    @nlg:en any other non-criminal (civil, labour, electoral ...) judicial proceeding
    `processo administrativo disciplinar`
    @nlg:en an administrative disciplinary proceeding
    `outro processo administrativo`
    @nlg:en any other administrative proceeding
    `inquérito civil`
    @nlg:en a civil inquiry (conducted by the public prosecution)
    `juízo arbitral`
    @nlg:en an arbitration
    `nenhum processo ou procedimento`
    @nlg:en no proceeding at all

-- "processo judicial": every judicial proceeding, of whatever branch. An
-- action for administrative impropriety is a judicial action.
GIVEN p IS A `Processo ou procedimento`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the proceeding is a judicial proceeding
`é processo judicial` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `processo judicial penal`         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ação de improbidade administrativa` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `outro processo judicial não penal` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "processo civil" (arts. 342, § 1º; 343, parágrafo único; 347): a judicial
-- proceeding that is not criminal.
GIVEN p IS A `Processo ou procedimento`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the proceeding is a civil, that is non-criminal, judicial proceeding
`é processo civil` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `ação de improbidade administrativa` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `outro processo judicial não penal` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "processo administrativo" (arts. 342, 344, 347): a disciplinary proceeding
-- is one. The investigations the public prosecution conducts (the
-- procedimento investigatório criminal and the inquérito civil) are not
-- counted as "processo administrativo": art. 339, worded in 2020, names them
-- beside "processo administrativo disciplinar", which it would not need to do
-- if they were administrative proceedings; fork F-g6b-09.
GIVEN p IS A `Processo ou procedimento`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the proceeding is an administrative proceeding
`é processo administrativo` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `processo administrativo disciplinar` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `outro processo administrativo`       THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Quem funciona no processo`

-- The persons the chapter names as acting in a proceeding. Each article lists
-- its own: art. 342 the one who testifies ("testemunha, perito, contador,
-- tradutor ou intérprete"), art. 343 the one bribed (the same five), art. 357
-- the one influence is pretended over ("juiz, jurado, órgão do Ministério
-- Público, funcionário de justiça, perito, tradutor, intérprete ou
-- testemunha", which does not name the contador). A party to the proceeding,
-- or anyone else, is recorded as one of the last two members, which no
-- article's list names.
DECLARE `Pessoa que funciona no processo` IS ONE OF
    juiz
    @nlg:en a judge
    jurado
    @nlg:en a juror
    `órgão do Ministério Público`
    @nlg:en a member of the public prosecution
    `funcionário de justiça`
    @nlg:en a court official
    perito
    @nlg:en an expert
    contador
    @nlg:en an accountant
    tradutor
    @nlg:en a translator
    `intérprete`
    @nlg:en an interpreter
    testemunha
    @nlg:en a witness
    `parte no processo`
    @nlg:en a party to the proceeding
    `pessoa sem função no processo`
    @nlg:en someone with none of these roles in the proceeding
